      "There's a certain kind of friendship that never disagrees, never challenges, never risks discomfort. Everything is smooth. Everything is \"fine.\" Nothing difficult is ever said. And those friendships never last. They collapse under the weight of everything that was left unsaid — because avoiding hard conversations is nothing more than delaying the truth. Whether you're leading Marines, raising a family, showing up for a brother, or standing inside a gym community that demands excellence, one principle holds steady: Good friends don't let you drift. Good friends don't let you lie to yourself. Good friends have hard conversations.",
