      "Nobody wakes up excited to practice what they're bad at. Motivation usually follows success, not the other way around. The early stages of improvement are frustrating and slow. Your progress feels invisible. You question whether the effort is worth it. This is where discipline takes over. Discipline says: do the work anyway. Five extra minutes of mobility. Three extra sets of skill practice. One more attempt at the movement that exposed your weakness. Stack those days long enough, and the impossible begins to feel manageable.",
